      "id": "AWS-SNS-02",
      "title": "SNS batching: the default BatchSize fills 10-entry PublishBatch calls under a steady stream; Interval flushes a partial batch once the stream is idle; entries carry a Subject",
      "tier": "aws",
      "priority": "P1",
      "intent": "Batching is how SFC keeps SNS request counts down - one PublishBatch carries up to ten messages - and Interval is what bounds the latency of a partial batch. SnsBatch leaves BatchSize at its documented default of 10 (AwsSnsTargetConfiguration.kt:91-92,170) and gets a record every 100 ms, so it must flush full ten-entry batches (AwsSnsTargetWriter.kt:214-216); its Interval of 2000 ms never elapses between two records. SnsIdle gets a record every second with BatchSize 10 and Interval 200, so only the timer (:169-172) can flush it, one record at a time. SnsBatch also sets a Subject on every entry (:362-364); the raw-delivery subscription drops SNS metadata, so the case proves only that the real service accepts ten-entry batches carrying a Subject, not its value. Both publish to the stack topic and are told apart by schedule. The case fails if batching is off or the default changes (Messages/Writes would be 1, about 10 is expected), if the Interval flush does not happen (a Slow record would wait for ten, 10 s), if SNS rejects an entry ('Error sending message'), or if records are lost or duplicated. That Interval is an inactivity timer rather than a maximum wait is pinned by AWS-SNS-DEF-01.",
      "pins": [
        "targets/aws-sns-target/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/awssns/AwsSnsTargetWriter.kt:153-180",
        "targets/aws-sns-target/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/awssns/AwsSnsTargetWriter.kt:214-216",
        "targets/aws-sns-target/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/awssns/AwsSnsTargetWriter.kt:362-364",
        "targets/aws-sns-target/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/awssns/config/AwsSnsTargetConfiguration.kt:82-92",
        "targets/aws-sns-target/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/awssns/config/AwsSnsTargetConfiguration.kt:133-139",
        "targets/aws-sns-target/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/awssns/config/AwsSnsTargetConfiguration.kt:170"
      ],
      "sinks": {
        "main": {
          "kind": "sns"
        }
      },
      "records": 34,
      "timeoutSeconds": 90,
      "offlineSeconds": 25,
      "steps": [
        {
          "wait": {
            "metric": {
              "source": "SnsIdle",
              "name": "Writes",
              "op": "ge",
              "value": 4
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "wait": {
            "metric": {
              "source": "SnsBatch",
              "name": "Writes",
              "op": "ge",
              "value": 3
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "recordCount",
          "where": {
            "schedule": "Slow"
          },
          "min": 4
        },
        {
          "kind": "recordCount",
          "where": {
            "schedule": "Fast"
          },
          "min": 20
        },
        {
          "kind": "channelValueRun",
          "where": {
            "schedule": "Slow"
          },
          "source": "simSlow",
          "channel": "ctr"
        },
        {
          "kind": "channelValueRun",
          "where": {
            "schedule": "Fast"
          },
          "source": "simFast",
          "channel": "ctr"
        },
        {
          "kind": "metricRatio",
          "numerator": {
            "source": "SnsBatch",
            "name": "Messages"
          },
          "denominator": {
            "source": "SnsBatch",
            "name": "Writes"
          },
          "op": "ge",
          "value": 6,
          "comment": "default BatchSize 10: full batches of 10; 1 would mean no batching, 6 leaves room for a start-up partial"
        },
        {
          "kind": "metricRatio",
          "numerator": {
            "source": "SnsIdle",
            "name": "Messages"
          },
          "denominator": {
            "source": "SnsIdle",
            "name": "Writes"
          },
          "op": "lt",
          "value": 2,
          "comment": "the 200 ms timer flushes each slow record (the start-up reads can share a write); without it a write would carry 10"
        },
        {
          "kind": "logAbsent",
          "texts": [
            "Error sending to topic",
            "Error sending message"
          ]
        }
      ],
